{:id :EACL-FORMAL-078
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :manual-review
 :seed-or-trace "eacl-rust BUGS.md EACL-RS-103"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :availability
 :affected-versions
 ["v8.0.0 commit a698b3bdf15e61be9bfd1324d7d7c67dc82176be"]
 :affected-backends [:shared]
 :root-cause
 "validate-value counted a collection's entries by reducing every child first and compared the total with maximum-entries only afterwards. A huge collection was walked completely before it was rejected, and an unbounded lazy sequence was never rejected, so encode-canonical, canonicalize, capture-portable, and every digest built on them did not return."
 :fix
 "validate-value threads one running entry count through the whole value and checks it before each value is examined, so validation visits at most maximum-entries + 1 values and fails with :too-many-entries."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.secure-format-test/validation-work-is-bounded-by-maximum-entries-test (CLJ and CLJS)"]}
